# Internal docs — working notes, deliberately not part of this repo. It is a
# public, browsable portfolio; these are not for it.
#
# READ THIS BEFORE TRUSTING THE LINES BELOW. Listing a path here does nothing
# if the path is already tracked: git consults .gitignore only for untracked
# paths. Every doc below was listed here for months while still being committed
# and pushed, and nothing warned about it. To verify this file is actually
# doing its job:
#
#     git ls-files | git check-ignore --stdin --no-index
#
# Whatever that prints is ignored AND tracked — i.e. still being published.
# Untrack it with `git rm --cached <path>` (keeps your local copy).
# The --no-index flag is essential: without it check-ignore consults the index
# and stays silent about precisely the files that are broken.
AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.md
Handoff.md
antlii-*.md
